meta {
  name: Key beep off
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/beep?on=0
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200 { beepOnKeys: false }

  Read-or-set, same shape as /nogo. GET /beep just reports the current
  value; POST /beep?on=1 re-enables.

  Stored under its own NVS key ("wifi"/"beepkeys"), NOT in the cfg blob:
  adding a field to Config changes sizeof(Config) and loadConfig deletes
  any blob whose size does not match, which would wipe username,
  speedUnit, timezoneOffsetHours and otaCheckOnStart on every
  already-provisioned device. Default is ON when the key is absent.

  Same setting as the "Key beep : ON/OFF" row on the device CONFIG
  screen — either one updates the other.

  Turn it back on with POST /beep?on=1.
}
